course: biology
lesson: 399
title: Bites, stings and scratches: mosquitoes, wasps, ticks, dog bites and cat scratches
level: primary-4
stars: 2
explain: A summer night, an open window, and in the morning your arm is covered in itchy red bumps. A mosquito had dinner while you slept, and the itch is your body reacting to its spit.
explain: Most bites and stings are animals defending themselves or feeding: a bee stings when squashed, a dog bites when it is scared or someone takes its bone, a cat scratches when its tail is pulled. Almost all of them warn you first, if you know how to read the signs.
explain: The best protection is respect: do not grab, squeeze or corner animals, ask the owner before stroking a dog, leave nests alone and check your skin after walks in long grass.
explain: And after any bite or sting, the first step is always the same: tell a grown-up straight away. A grown-up decides whether it needs a wash and a cool cloth, a doctor or an emergency call.
fact: Only female mosquitoes bite, because they need blood to make their eggs; their spit keeps the blood runny so it does not clot, and our body reacts to the spit with an itchy bump, which scratching makes itch even more.
fact: A mosquito's mouth is not one needle but six thin parts working together.
fact: A honeybee's sting has barbs and stays in the skin, so the bee dies after stinging, while a wasp's sting is smooth and can sting again; a grown-up scrapes a bee sting out with a fingernail or card, and cold water and a cool cloth help.
fact: A few people have a strong allergic reaction to stings that can swell the face and make breathing hard; that is an emergency, and in Ukraine and across Europe the emergency number is 112.
fact: A tick bite usually does not hurt, so ticks are often found later; a grown-up should take one out close to the skin with a tick tool, and a spreading red ring days later means a doctor should check it.
fact: Most dog bites happen with dogs people know, often when the dog is eating, sleeping or hurt; growling, a stiff body and showing teeth are warnings that mean back off.
fact: Always ask the owner before stroking a dog, and let the dog sniff you first.
fact: Cats scratch and bite when scared or hurt and usually warn first with flattened ears and a swishing tail; a scratch should be washed with soap and water, and a doctor should look if it swells, gets hot or the person feels ill.
fact: Horseflies cut the skin with blade-like mouthparts and lap up the blood, so the bite hurts more than a mosquito's; they are drawn to dark moving things and warm bodies.
fact: Red wood ants bite and spray a stinging acid from their back end to defend their nest mounds, which can hold hundreds of thousands of ants; it stings but is not dangerous.
fact: Almost all spiders in Ukraine and Europe are harmless to people, most cannot even bite through our skin, and they bite only when trapped or squeezed; a spider has two fangs, eight legs and often eight eyes.
fact: After any bite or sting, tell a grown-up straight away, wash with soap and water and keep the hurt part still and cool; never try to catch or kill the animal, a photo from a safe distance is enough.
exercise: Which mosquitoes bite? | Only the females | Only the males | Only the babies | All mosquitoes equally
exercise: Why do female mosquitoes need blood? | To make their eggs | To keep warm at night | To grow their wings | To make honey
exercise: What makes a mosquito bite itch? | Our body reacting to the mosquito's spit | A tiny egg that the mosquito left under the skin | The mosquito's sharp teeth | Poison from the mosquito's wings
exercise: Why does a honeybee die after stinging? | Its barbed sting stays in the skin | It runs out of air because it holds its breath to sting | It gets squashed every time | It is too tired to fly home
exercise: Which can sting more than once? | A wasp | A honeybee | Both only once | Neither can sting
exercise: What helps after a bee sting, once a grown-up has scraped it out? | Cold water and a cool cloth | Hot sand rubbed hard into the sting | Squeezing it hard | Leaving the sting in
exercise: What is the emergency number in Ukraine and across Europe? | 112 | 999 only | 123 | 000
exercise: Why are ticks often found only later? | A tick bite usually does not hurt | Ticks are completely invisible to our eyes | Ticks bite only at night | Ticks hide deep inside the skin
exercise: What sign days after a tick bite means a doctor should check it? | A spreading red ring around the bite | A tiny dry spot that falls off | A small itch that soon fades away again | A bruise from bumping it
exercise: When do most dog bites happen? | With dogs people know, often when the dog is eating, sleeping or hurt | Only with wild dogs that live in the woods and have never met people before | Only when dogs are playing fetch | Only with puppies
exercise: Which of these is a warning that a dog might bite? | Growling | Wagging loosely | Rolling over to play | Sleeping quietly
exercise: What should you do before stroking a dog you do not know? | Ask the owner and let the dog sniff you first | Hug it straight away so it knows that you are friendly | Run up to it fast | Pat it on the head from behind
exercise: How does a cat warn you to leave it alone? | Flattened ears and a swishing tail | Loud purring and slow blinking | Rolling over on its back | Rubbing on your legs
exercise: Why does a horsefly bite hurt more than a mosquito's? | It cuts the skin with blade-like mouthparts | It squirts hot water under the skin | It has bigger teeth than a dog | It bites three times at once
exercise: What do red wood ants spray to defend their nest? | A stinging acid | Sticky honey | Very cold water | Fine silk threads
exercise: Are most spiders in Europe dangerous to people? | No, almost all are harmless | Yes, every one is dangerous | Yes, if they are black | Only the small ones are harmless
exercise: What is the first step after any bite or sting? | Tell a grown-up straight away | Catch the animal | Wait and say nothing | Scratch it hard
test: «got 6 bites last night, them male mozzies are evil» What is wrong? | Only female mosquitoes bite | Mosquitoes do not bite at night | Males bite more than females | Mosquitoes never bite people
test: «it itches like mad, gonna scratch till it bleeds» What is the best advice? | Scratching makes it itch more, so leave it and use a cool cloth | Scratching hard makes the itch go away for good, so keep going | Scratch it with a stick instead | Scratching removes all the spit
test: A girl at school carries a special pen in case of a wasp sting. After a sting she struggles to breathe. What should happen? | A grown-up calls 112 at once | Wait quietly to see if it passes | Give her a drink of juice and some biscuits | Tell her to run around
test: In a cartoon, a bee stings a bear on the nose again and again. What is wrong for a honeybee? | A honeybee can sting only once and then dies | Bees can sting a hundred times, but only big animals like bears | Bees never sting bears | Bees sting with their teeth
test: «found a tick on me after camping, I'll just squeeze it off» What is better? | Tell a grown-up, who takes it out close to the skin with a tick tool | Squeeze its body hard between two fingers until it lets go of the skin | Leave it there for a week | Burn it with a match
test: Count them: a spider has 8 legs and 2 fangs. How many legs and fangs do 3 spiders have? | 24 legs and 6 fangs | 24 legs and 3 fangs | 18 legs and 6 fangs | 32 legs and 8 fangs
test: «every spider in Europe can kill ya» What is the best correction? | Almost all are harmless, and most cannot even bite through our skin | True, all spiders are deadly, even the little ones in the bath | True, but only in summer | Spiders have no fangs at all
test: Your friend's dog growls and goes stiff when you reach for its bone. What should you do? | Back off and leave the dog and the bone alone | Grab the bone quickly before the dog can bite you | Stare hard into its eyes | Pat it on the head
test: «Tom always pulls the cat's tail in the cartoon and the cat's fine» What would a real cat do? | Scratch or bite because it is scared or hurt | Laugh about it and run away | Purr happily | Pull Tom's tail back
test: The cat scratch on your hand is now swollen, hot and you feel ill. What should happen? | A doctor should look at it | Nothing, scratches always heal | Put more soap on it every hour | Scratch it again to clean it
test: «sat on a mound in the woods and now my legs are on fire» What has probably happened? | Red wood ants bit and sprayed acid to defend their nest | A snake was hiding in the mound and bit you lots of times | Hornets stung you | The mound was hot from the Sun
test: «a weird bug bit me, I'm gonna catch it and bring it in a jar» What is the best plan? | Tell a grown-up and take a photo from a safe distance instead | Catch it with your bare hand and keep it in the jar for the doctor | Squash it and keep it | Let it bite again to check
exam: Identify the reason for which only female mosquitoes consume blood. | They require blood for the production of their eggs | They require blood in order to maintain their body temperature | They require blood for the growth of their wings | Blood constitutes the sole food of all mosquitoes
exam: Which of the following statements most accurately characterises the sting of the honeybee in comparison with that of the wasp? | The barbed sting of the honeybee remains in the skin, whereas the smooth sting of the wasp may be employed repeatedly | The sting of the wasp remains in the skin, whereas that of the honeybee may be withdrawn and employed repeatedly against an intruder | Both insects may sting only once | Neither insect possesses a sting
exam: Select the response consistent with the established guidance following any bite or sting received by a child. | An adult shall be informed forthwith, and the affected part washed and kept still and cool | The animal responsible shall be captured and retained | The child shall refrain from informing any person | The affected part shall be scratched vigorously
exam: It is given that a spider possesses eight legs and two fangs. Ascertain the total number of legs of four spiders. | Thirty-two | Twenty-four | Eight | Sixteen
